    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0413" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/3737: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dennis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-03T14:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1925—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 4—11:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. Referring to the Department’s telegram of May 29, 5 p.m. The Honduranean
                    Government has sent instructions to Lainez<anchor n="24" xml:id="d288-f1"/> to
                    make appropriate representations to the Guatemalan Government on the basis of
                    the Ferrera letters, fresh invasions, and the findings of a commission of
                    investigation along the border. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Repeated to Guatemala and Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dennis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="24" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>Silverio Lainez, Honduran Minister to Guatemala.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
